  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Vetjet Fuels has $337M in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. Vetjet Fuels won 271 awards so far this fiscal year with an average award size of $1.2M, and obligations are up 94.2% year over year. Obligations increased from $2.7M in FY21 to $4.1M in FY22, $9.4M in FY23, $69M in FY24, and $174M in FY25 before reaching $337M in FY26. The Department of Defense is the largest buying agency, accounting for $337M in obligations in FY2026 to date. Petroleum Refineries is the largest NAICS market with $337M in obligations in FY2026 to date. Current-year totals are fiscal year to date and are partial. All figures are contract obligations except award-value figures in the largest-awards and expiring-contracts tables, which are total contract values.",
